- `pekko-serialization` provides the registry, manifests, ids (user ids from 41), and the error taxonomy (`spi/serializer.go`, `serialization/registry.go`). It has no primitive serializers (README says so); adding int32/int64/string/bool/bytes serializers is the concrete piece Typed would need there. It has no `serialize-messages` check mode.
- `pekko-observability` is an empty scaffold (`go.mod` without requires, `spi/doc.go`, `internal/doc.go`). Instrumentation hooks must be defined in `pekko-actor`.
- `kit-logger` v0.2.0: `Logger` has `With`, `WithContext`, `SetLevel`; `Config.GlobalFields` are static; dynamic fields need `SetContextFieldExtractor`. Its mock (`kitlogtest.MockLogger`) drops the arguments of `With`/`WithContext`, makes `SetLevel` a no-op and exposes `Entries` without a lock. A per-actor logger and MDC mapping (`withMdc`, `logMessages`) cannot be asserted with it as is; a purpose-built fake or adapter is needed. `Config.Logger` is nil-silent. Real `Sampling` and `RateLimit` can drop entries silently, so tests must use the mock. `golang.org/x/time` in `pekko-actor/go.mod` is an indirect dependency of kit-logger, not used by actor code.
- `go-specs` v0.4.0 offers `Eventually`/`Consistently`, `mock.Spy`, `mock.Controller` and `Captor`, but nothing actor-specific: `TestProbe`, `TestInbox` and `BehaviorTestKit` must be built in goPekko, and only in test-support code.

